gs, maybe the pod isn't configured to expose metrics, or the metrics endpoint is down. \n\nSince the DNS error is specific to the user-service, looking into its logs and configuration (like environment variables or config maps) would be crucial. They might also need to check the service definitions for user-service to ensure they're correctly pointing to Prometheus. \n\nThe next tool call should be to get the logs of the user-service pod to inspect for any errors or misconfigurations that could explain the DNS resolution failure and the missing metrics.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-hjhqb -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-be72023842819deb', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 482, 'prompt_tokens': 4196, 'total_tokens': 4678, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdcc-0b8c-7332-a66b-4e3fd1809777-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs user-service-559b79c875-hjhqb -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-be72023842819deb', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4196, 'output_tokens': 482, 'total_tokens': 4678}), ToolMessage(content="[2026-Mar-17 21:52:37.887617] <info>: (UserHandler.h:932:GetMachineId) MAC address = 0a:54:4f:39:17:7f\n[2026-Mar-17 21:52:37.887886] <info>: (UserService.cpp:63:main) machine_id = 316\n[2026-Mar-17 21:52:38.189174] <error>: (utils_mongodb.h:76:CreateIndex) Error in createIndexes: No suitable servers found: `serverSelectionTimeoutMS` expired: [unknown connection error calling ismaster on 'user-mongodb:27017']\n[2026-Mar-17 21:52:38.189354