I should verify the MongoDB service\'s endpoints. Maybe the service isn\'t correctly pointing to the pods, or there\'s a misconfiguration in the service YAML. Also, checking the network policies or firewall rules might be necessary, but since the user is in a Kubernetes cluster, maybe the service is misconfigured.\n\nAnother angle: the logs show the pod is running, but the MongoDB connection is failing. So the issue is likely with the MongoDB service itself. Let me check the user-mongodb pods first. If they\'re not running, that\'s the root cause. If they are running, maybe the service isn\'t properly set up, or there\'s a port issue. Also, checking the MongoDB pods\' logs could reveal if the service is starting correctly and listening on the right port.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl get pods -n social-network | grep user-mongodb"  \nThe logs indicate the `user-service` pod is failing to connect to `user-mongodb`. To confirm if the `user-mongodb` service is running and healthy, I need to check the status of its associated pods. If the MongoDB pods are not running or are in a crash loop, that would explain the connection failures. This command will filter the list of pods to focus on `user-mongodb`-related components.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 437, 'prompt_tokens': 5421, 'total_tokens': 5858, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdcc-24f9-7272-bf3f-5e5c82b151c8-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5421, 'output_tokens': 437, 'total_tokens': 5858}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4dc72919-27e4-4bcb-adb9-59460287a244'), AIMessage(content