rrect, leading to an error. The LLM had to adjust the submission format, which shows a minor oversight in adhering to the tool\'s requirements. Also, the initial patching step might have been redundant since the service was already correctly configured, but it\'s part of the process.\n</think>\n\nThe `user-mongodb` service and pod are missing from all namespaces, indicating a deployment or configuration error. To confirm, we need to check if the pod exists in any namespace using `--all-namespaces`. If the pod is absent, the issue likely stems from a deployment or configuration error, requiring further investigation into the pod\'s creation or service binding.\n\nNext step: Generate a tool call to list all pods across namespaces.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=485, prompt_tokens=7910, total_tokens=8395, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfdd2-f88a-7792-a20b-9dc652c471c5-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7910, 'output_tokens': 485, 'total_tokens': 8395}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ee6de4af-f95f-4042-8d0b-8e4b9d98b643')]]
